      "writtenOn": "2025-06-26T22:28:16Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Ahh thanks, I get it. Definitely makes sense that if you call WaitAny() on a future then WaitAny() shouldn\u0027t return until the callback is complete, even if the callback was triggered from somewhere else. We should spec this (https://github.com/webgpu-native/webgpu-headers/blob/main/doc/articles/Asynchronous%20Operations.md).\n\nThat said I think this CL will affect ProcessEvents too, and I don\u0027t think we want that because the callback could be long-running and ProcessEvents has a global list of events.\nIt might affect Spontaneous too (which would be a bigger problem) if we ever can have two threads attempt to SetFutureReady the same future. I\u0027m not sure if that happens in practice.",
      "parentUuid": "5c892350_96512b26",
      "revId": "cda86a85a50b6f85e750661624d1124bb1ff7157",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
